patel.codes/goard is an opinionated, modern
CLI for managing a local go module cache.

i recommend `GOMEMLIMIT=<0.75 * main memory>`
when running this program.

flags:
  -index   update the index only, no downloads

layout (~/.goard):
  index.json   feed cursor
  fetch.jsonl  append-only module path log; compacts on exit
  large.jsonl  debug only (>128 MiB decompressed modules)
  modules/     GOMODCACHE layout
  tmp/         staging, wiped at startup

using brtfs on a remote machine,

```
sudo truncate -s 700G /corpus.img
DEV=$(sudo losetup --find --show --direct-io=on /corpus.img)
sudo mkfs.btrfs -q "$DEV"
mkdir -p ~/.goard
sudo mount -o noatime,compress=zstd:3 "$DEV" ~/.goard
sudo chown "$USER" ~/.goard
```

then, build the index:
  ./goard -index 2>&1 | tee index.log

and, download the modules:
  GOMEMLIMIT=<lim> nohup ./goard > pull.log 2>&1 &

this repository was original a set of patches
over https://github.com/FiloSottile/mostly-harmless/tree/main/allcode
but diverged and became its own program here.
